For \(a = 1,\; b = 2,\; c = 3\):

\[
x=\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{\,b^{2}-4ac\,}}{2a}
   =\frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{\,4-12\,}}{2}
   =\frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{-8}}{2}
   =\frac{-2 \pm i\,\sqrt{8}}{2}
   =-1 \pm i\,\sqrt{2}.
\]

So the quadratic has two complex conjugate roots:

\[
\boxed{x=-1+i\sqrt{2}\quad\text{and}\quad x=-1-i\sqrt{2}}
\]

There are no real solutions because the discriminant \(b^{2}-4ac = -8 < 0\).
